  <title id="bdl31sinemanifold-title">Samples and exact density of the function-space prior of a one-parameter sine network</title>
  <desc id="bdl31sinemanifold-desc">Left: four hundred Monte Carlo samples of (F1, F2) = (sin theta, sin 2 theta) with theta drawn from a standard normal distribution; all points lie on a closed one-dimensional curve in the square from minus one to one, running from the lower left through the origin to the upper right, with outer arcs near F1 equal to plus or minus one. Right: the same curve shaded by the induced density p(theta) divided by the norm of the derivative of the map, on a scale from 0 to 0.4; the density is highest near the minimum at the lower left and the maximum at the upper right and fades to almost zero along the outer arcs.</desc>
